; exit 72 (see .exit)
; ABORT TO AN ARENA MARK, for the division trap.
;
; `(__axiom_recover mark thunk)` arms a recovery point at `mark` and
; runs `thunk`. The three traps - 70 out of memory, 71 unhandled
; effect, 72 division by zero - stop being the end of the process
; INSIDE such an extent: the arena is reset to the mark, the effect
; slots are restored, the stack pointer is put back, and the arming
; call answers the trap's status instead of returning.
;
; Both halves are here on purpose, because only one of them is new.
; The first division happens inside a recovery point and the program
; keeps running with the status in hand. The second happens with
; nothing armed, and then the trap does exactly what it did before
; recovery existed: the sentence in `.err` on fd 2, and 72 in `.exit`.
; A mechanism that recovered everywhere would be a worse language,
; not a better one - a divide by zero in a program that never asked
; to survive one must still stop the program.
;
; The second half is also the reason both halves have to be in ONE
; case. With `__axiom_recover` unreferenced the whole mechanism is
; dead code: the helper is internal and deleted, no store to
; `@__axiom_recover_top` survives, and GlobalOpt folds the armed test
; in the trap to false. A fixture that only ever traps outside an
; extent would therefore test a trap with no branch in it.
;
; The divisor comes from a function so that no constant folding can
; decide it before the guard does - the same reason
; `tests/selfhost/980-divide-by-zero.ax` gives.
(import IO)

(import Str)

(:: zero Int)

(fn (zero) 0)

(:: divide (-> Int Int))

(fn (divide x) (/ 10 zero))

(:: main Int)

;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (main)
  (let ((inside 
    (__axiom_recover
      __axiom_arena_mark      (lambda (x) (divide x))
    )
  ))
    {
      (println "recovered {inside}")
      ; Outside every recovery point: this one is the end of the
      ; program, and the two lines after it never run.
      (divide 0)
      ; Spelled `printlnLit` and not `println` for the reason
      ; `314-out-of-memory.ax` spells its own unreachable line that
      ; way: `verify-stdlib-out.py` MODELS `(println "literal")` as a
      ; claim that the literal appears in the golden, and this line is
      ; deliberately never printed. It is still a tripwire - if the
      ; trap outside a recovery point ever stops stopping the program,
      ; stdout gains a line and the golden says so.
      (printlnLit (strCStr "UNREACHABLE: the trap outside a recovery point returned"))
    }
  )
)
